@* Fitment confirmation bar above the PDP. Green = confirmed fit for the active vehicle.
   Sits at the top of the page because "does this fit my car?" is the first question a
   parts customer asks.

   TODO (data): the fits/doesn't-fit determination and the vehicle description come from
   the product's fitment lookup against VehicleFitmentState. Change Vehicle should clear
   the active vehicle the same way VehiclePicked does. *@

<div class="fitment-banner @(Fits ? "fitment-banner--fits" : "fitment-banner--unknown") @Class" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">
    <span class="fitment-banner-status">
        <span class="fitment-banner-icon" aria-hidden="true">@(Fits ? "✓" : "!")</span>
        @if (Fits)
        {
            <span>This Fits Your <strong>@VehicleDescription</strong></span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span>Select a vehicle to confirm this fits</span>
        }
    </span>

    <span class="fitment-banner-actions">
        <SfButton Variant="SfButtonVariant.Ghost" Size="SfButtonSize.Sm" @onclick="OnMoreProducts">
            More Products
            <span class="fitment-banner-caret" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span>
        </SfButton>

        <span class="fitment-banner-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>

        <SfButton Variant="SfButtonVariant.Ghost" Size="SfButtonSize.Sm" @onclick="OnChangeVehicle">
            <span class="fitment-banner-refresh" aria-hidden="true">⟳</span>
            Change Vehicle
        </SfButton>
    </span>
</div>
